# RealData passwords

`passwordHash` lives in the RealData tab, in a fixed column, next to names and bios. A shifted column writes the next profile save into the wrong cell and locks people out. The sheet will not warn you.

- Do not insert, delete, reorder, or rewrite RealData columns. Do not run `values.clear`, a full-tab `values.update`, or a header rewrite on that tab.
- Do not set `passwordHash` to empty on a person who already has one. Profile edits copy the hash already on the sheet.
- Add a field only by appending it to `PEOPLE_HEADERS` in `scripts/sheet-schema.js`, then backfilling cells. Never put a new column in the middle.
- Write people through `upsertRealDataRecord`. It refuses a header row that does not match the schema column-for-column, and it refuses to blank an existing hash.
- Claim, password reset, and password change may replace a hash with a new non-empty hash. They go through `server/directory-auth.js`.
- Do not print password hashes, service-account keys, or roster emails in chat, logs, or commits.
